{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1564238-looking-for-a-legacy-about-unlocking-doors-gates-and-personal-transformation","id":1564238,"title":"Looking for a Legacy about unlocking doors, gates and personal transformation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-09-21T07:11:19-07:00","id":1564238,"title":"Looking for a Legacy about unlocking doors, gates and personal transformation","content":"So, my character Key, a biracial transwoman from New Orleans, is an Adamantine Arrow Mastigos. She signed her name to the Watchtower of Burning Iron after defeating her opiate addiction and claiming the prize. She is still recovering, and she returned from the Mastigos Watchtower with an uncharacteristic Golden Key (curious!).<br /> <br /> She just hit Gnosis 3, and I am now considering Legacies. Having Weaponry 3 with a specialty in Swords, the obvious choice for a Legacy is Brotherhood of the Demon Wind (although I will be calling it the Demon Wind school if I do join), but I really like the idea of keys, doors, and how crossing liminal spaces changes and transforms those who go through, also playing with the ideas of initiation and transformation. I've been looking at the various fan written Legacies. While the Reality Stalkers and House of the Ariadne also appeal, a legacy about travelers, gates and personal spiritual transformations and overcoming challenges appeals to Key's Adamantine Arrow heritage.<br /> <br /> Any anyone help a girl out? (irl, I am Cis :P)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T13:21:24-07:00","id":1564251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Armsley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1564238-looking-for-a-legacy-about-unlocking-doors-gates-and-personal-transformation#post1564238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, my character Key, a biracial transwoman from New Orleans, is an Adamantine Arrow Mastigos. She signed her name to the Watchtower of Burning Iron after defeating her opiate addiction and claiming the prize. She is still recovering, and she returned from the Mastigos Watchtower with an uncharacteristic Golden Key (curious!).<br /> <br /> She just hit Gnosis 3, and I am now considering Legacies. Having Weaponry 3 with a specialty in Swords, the obvious choice for a Legacy is Brotherhood of the Demon Wind (although I will be calling it the Demon Wind school if I do join), but I really like the idea of keys, doors, and how crossing liminal spaces changes and transforms those who go through, also playing with the ideas of initiation and transformation. I've been looking at the various fan written Legacies. While the Reality Stalkers and House of the Ariadne also appeal, a legacy about travelers, gates and personal spiritual transformations and overcoming challenges appeals to Key's Adamantine Arrow heritage.<br /> <br /> Any anyone help a girl out? (irl, I am Cis :P)</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1557627-the-crystal-navigators-a-mastigos-legacy-of-free-spirited-pirates\">Crystal Navigators</a>, who are all about adventure and pushing your understanding of your free will as far as possible.<br /> <br /> I think the Clavicularius might also be a good fit, they are the Keepers of the Key, their philosophy is all about personal transformation and self improvement. They have a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1341513-2e-legacy-update-clavicularius\">2ed conversion</a> already, I also have an alternative set of Attainments I could share, if you would like. Both Legacies have Mastigos as their parent Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T18:54:40-07:00","id":1564259,"title":"","content":"I'd have probably gone with the Clavicularius. But I think 2e really encourages you to kind of make your own legacy, so you might whip up something yourself that fits what you want from the concept.<br /> <br /> It shouldn't take too much work for the basics you'll need and would give you something more personal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T22:26:12-07:00","id":1564263,"title":"","content":"One of the other players in the chronicle wants to go for Clavicarius, and I am not sure my PC agrees with their approach. See, she wants to turn her Vices into Virtues, and use Virtues as tools. For example, taking the Geotia of her substance use disorder (&quot;addiction&quot; is not a medical term) and turning it into a being of recovery earned via personal transformation and overcoming the challenges of using opiates.<br /> <br /> I was also wanting to fool around with actual gateways, doors, keys, space magic stuff. Hrm. I'll need to think about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-22T03:33:08-07:00","id":1564268,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:15px\">How about something like this ? Fate primary, Space optional, themed on traveling the paths of synchronicity and that there is no distinction between physically and metaphysically making your way in the world.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Fate 1</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\">A Compelling of Fate that nudges events to ensure the subject is at the right place at the right time, replicating </span><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Green Light, Red Light.</i></span><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Reach is assigned to advanced duration.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Space 1</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Interconnections</i></span><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> with Reach assigned to advanced duration and conjunctional Space 1 allowing them to understand the emotional character of sympathetic connections in broad terms. It allows them to perceive connections and paths forward others don't.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Fate 2</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Lucky Number</i></span><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> with Reach assigned to instant use.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Space 2</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Reading the Outmost Eddies </i></span><span style=\"font-size:15px\">with Reach assigned to instant use and advanced duration. With conjunctional Space 1, the right threads of fate are nudged closer, allowing results to be obtained in an hour.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Fate 3</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Serendipity</i></span><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> with Reach assigned to instant use and using any skill.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Space 3</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Break Boundary</i></span><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> with Reach assigned to instant use and passing through narrow paths.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Fate 4</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Strings of Fate</i></span><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> with Reach assigned to advanced duration. With conjunctional Space 3, you can find the right thread of fate to get results in an hour.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Space 4</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Teleportation</i></span><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> with Reach assigned to instant use.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Fate 5</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Forge Destiny</i></span><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> with Reach assigned to advanced duration. Since you can give yourself Aspirations, Obsessions and Destiny's without Dooms, it serves for both the symbolism of charting your course in life and changing who you are for the better.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Space 5</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Co-Location</i></span><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> with Reach assigned to sympathetic range, indefinite duration and advanced scale. A point of mana pays for Sympathetic Range, Everywhere and indefinite duration. With conjuctional Fate 2, a Key can be applied to it. Creates your own permanent, private travel network.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 09-22-2026, 07:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-22T05:03:33-07:00","id":1564269,"title":"","content":"Thank you so kindly! In my head, I'm playing around with a Legacy that can open any Iris (or call for a Clash of Wills) and emphasizes world travelling. Hrm, maybe my concept is too broad. There's all sorts of directions this can go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-22T05:18:28-07:00","id":1564271,"title":"","content":"Happy to help. One thing that helps me when creating Legacies is to make one phrase, with no commas or pauses, that defines your Legacy. Whenever creating a new section (Attainments, yatras, oblations, organization, etc), you always go back to it. If it matches the design phrase, you keep it, if it doesn't, you rework it. Coming up with the phrase helps distill your ideas and using it keeps you on theme. A few examples from my own Legacies:<br /> <br /> <b>Azure Cranes:</b> &quot;Medical care available anytime and anywhere&quot;<br /> <b>Anima Meccanica:</b> &quot;Inventing a better tomorrow today&quot;<br /> <b>Crystal Navigators: </b>&quot;Navigating our choices&quot;<br /> <br /> In the case of the one posted above, it was &quot;Making a path through the world&quot;. Hope that proves helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}